gular Material"},{"id":375501288,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzU1MDEyODg=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/labels/area:%20core","name":"area: core","color":"c7def8","default":false,"description":"Issues related to the framework runtime"}],"state":"closed","locked":true,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2017-06-30T20:14:05Z","updated_at":"2019-09-12T00:22:42Z","closed_at":"2017-07-07T15:46:42Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"#### Reproduction\r\n1. Clone https://github.com/jelbourn/material.angular.io/tree/potal-ngmodule-not-found-repro\r\n2. `npm i`\r\n3. `npm run start`\r\n\r\n#### Error\r\n```\r\nERROR in Unexpected value 'PortalModule in /usr/local/google/home/jelbourn/material.angular.io/node_modules/@angular/material/material.d.ts' imported by the module 'DocViewerModule in /usr/local/google/home/jelbourn/material.angular.io/src/app/shared/doc-viewer/doc-viewer-module.ts'. Please add a @NgModule annotation.\r\n```\r\n\r\nWe moved `PortalModule` from `@angular/material` to `@angular/cdk`, along with a re-export in in the original location:\r\n```ts\r\nexport {TemplatePortalDirective, PortalHostDirective, PortalModule} from '@angular/cdk';\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt seems that the metadata isn't being seen through the re-export. I've tried adding both `\"flatModuleIndexRedirect\": true` and an `\"importAs\"` to the metadata.json in both packages, but this has no effect.\r\n\r\nUsing `4.2.5` for all angular/angular dependencies","closed_by":{"login":"jasonaden","id":516168,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNjE2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/516168?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jasonaden","html_url":"https://github.com/jasonaden","followers_url":"https://api.gi